receipt.\n32: 3. IF IT IS NOT an invoice (e.g. it is a person's photo, landscape, screenshot of a chat, unrelated document, or random text):\n33:    - Set is_valid_bill to false.\n34:    - Set rejection_reason explaining why (e.g. \"Uploaded image is not a financial bill or invoice\").\n35:    - Leave all financial fields null or empty.\n36: 4. IF IT IS AN INVOICE:\n37:    - Set is_valid_bill to true.\n38:    - Extract the EXACT vendor name, GSTIN, invoice number, date, and line items (description, qty, rate, amount) visible on the bill.\n39:    - NEVER make up or hallucinate missing data or dummy items. If a field (like GSTIN or invoice number) is not present or unreadable, set it to null and append it to unreadable_fields.\n40:    - Extract exact declared amounts; DO NOT fix math mistakes in the extraction.\n41: \n42: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\n43: {\n44:   \"is_valid_bill\": boolean,\n45:   \"rejection_reason\": string or null,\n46:   \"unreadable_fields\": [\"string\"],\n47:   \"vendor_name\": string or null,\n48:   \"vendor_address\": string or null,\n49:   \"gstin\": string or null,\n50:   \"invoice_no\": string or null,\n51:   \"date\": \"YYYY-MM-DD\" or null,\n52:   \"items\": [\n53:     {\n54:       \"description\": string,\n55:       \"hsn\": string or null,\n56:       \"qty\": number,\n57:       \"rate\": number,\n58:       \"amount\": number,\n59:       \"is_blurry\": boolean\n60:     }\n61:   ],\n62:   \"subtotal\": number or null,\n63:   \"cgst\": number or null,\n64:   \"sgst\": number or null,\n65:   \"igst\": number or null,\n66:   \"total_declared\": number or null,\n67:   \"bank_details\": {\n68:     \"bank_name\": string or null,\n69:     \"account_number\": string or null,\n70:     \"ifsc\": string or null\n71:   }\n72: }\n73: `;\n74: \n75: /**"}
